From 5835b7a796c25cf03063474682c8715bcb463991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:36:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The red and green slayer helmets, and membership by param

Batch 2 finished. Two of OSRS's eleven slayer helmet recolours are buildable here, and they are the
two whose monsters exist: red from an abyssal head, green from a Kq head.

WHY ONLY TWO. The other nine need the King Black Dragon - which is not a fightable npc in this
build, only a boss pet and a cutscene - or Vorkath, the Alchemical Hydra, Araxxor and five more
post-2013 bosses. Black comes free when batch 3 adds the KBD's model. The rest are out of era, and
inventing a source for a head that has no monster would have been worse than leaving them.

THE RECOLOUR IS CONFIG-LEVEL AND NEEDED NO ART. The helmet's face mask is the same two colours the
black mask itself is made of - rgb15 3170 and 5284 - so a variant is two recol pairs on the plain
helmet's own model. The destination values were found by searching the reachable rgb15 space for
the nearest paint to a target colour and then RENDERED before being written down, because a recol
source that matches no face leaves the helmet black with a coloured smear and the config gives no
error at all. Battery 67 re-checks both sources against the model's own face colours.

MEMBERSHIP IS THREE PARAMS NOW, NOT A LIST OF NAMES. ~black_mask_on_task, ~slayer_helm_worn and
~black_mask_imbued_on_task each listed the items they applied to. That list went from two to four
when the imbues landed yesterday and would have gone to ten today, in three places, with ten more
waiting behind bosses. So an item declares what it is - slayer_headgear for the melee bonus (both
masks and every helmet), slayer_helmet for the four protections a helmet inherits from its parts
(helmets only: a bare mask has no earmuffs in it), slayer_imbued for the ranged and magic boost -
and the three procs read that. Adding the black helmet in batch 3 needs no script edit at all.

A category would have been simpler still and cannot be used: an obj gets exactly one and these are
already armour_helmet, which the Entrana monk and the desert heat both read.

Drops and prices are OSRS's own: the abyssal head at 1/6,000 from abyssal demons, the Kq head at
1/128 from the Kalphite Queen, and both unlocks at 1,000 Slayer points. Unlike yesterday's imbue
price, none of these had to be invented - OSRS charges Slayer points for the recolours too.

Four objs generated rather than written, because it is not four: tools/genslayerhelm.py copies the
plain helmet and its imbued twin, changes the name and adds two recolour pairs, so a colour cannot
quietly have different stats from the helmet it is a recolour of.

Three things the checks caught that I had wrong:

  - the generator copied the plain helmet's params INCLUDING the slayer_* ones it then added
    itself, so every colour carried each param twice.
  - it emitted three [opheldu] triggers per colour - head-on-helmet and both helmets-on-head - and
    [opheldu,X] normalises the direction, so the extra two were duplicates and a duplicate trigger
    is a hard build error.
  - group 66's checks were written against the old name-list doors and had to be rewritten for the
    param design rather than left passing on text that no longer meant anything.

tools/poh_mutate_spec.py now drives genstores and genslayerhelm too, which is what lets the spec
mutations fail on their own named check instead of on "the generator is out of step".

Ten mutations, all red.

